This repository is derived from easthambuilds' recipe
https://github.com/easthambuilds/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold (Apache-2.0).
start.sh, stop.sh, scripts/, tools/, docker/Dockerfile and the .gitignore come from it. Changed here:
scripts/config.sh (the engine pin), scripts/common.sh (the image hash covers docker/patches/, rank 0's TF_FILL_*
settings), scripts/prepare.sh (model/chat_template.jinja put in place), scripts/local.sh.example (the TF_FILL_*
settings) and docker/Dockerfile (docker/patches/ applied to the Zig engine). README.md is new; it reuses parts of
the recipe's README.

docker/patches/ are changes to Bertholomus AI's TensorFold fork, branch deepseek-v41-zig
(https://github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold, Apache-2.0), itself a fork of TensorFold
(https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold, Apache-2.0). 0001-0004 are bertholomus/TensorFold #25, #28 (merged) and #29;
0005 is ours and not proposed upstream yet.

model/chat_template.jinja is the template the checkpoint easthambuilds/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-2.9bpw carries,
written by Mia's AI Lab as a port of DeepSeek's encoding/encoding.py (DeepSeek, MIT), with one change: each piece of
the prompt is written out as it is made instead of being added to one growing string.

The model weights (DeepSeek, MIT), the checkpoint, the engine, the kernel kit and NVIDIA's PyTorch container keep
their own licenses and terms; none of them is redistributed here.
